Subject: [dpadplay] gamescope headless: relax hasPrimary + /dev/dri render-node fallback

gamescope 3.16.19's CVulkanDevice::createDevice() queries VkPhysicalDeviceDrmPropertiesEXT
via vkGetPhysicalDeviceProperties2 and aborts the headless backend when drmProps.hasPrimary
is false ("physical device has no primary node") or drmProps.hasRender is false
("physical device has no render node").

On some driver/device/container combos (reproduced: UpCloud Helsinki NVIDIA L4, driver
580.173.02, CDI-injected /dev/dri, gamescope-WSI layer loaded) gamescope's query returns
drmProps entirely zeroed -- hasPrimary=false AND hasRender=false -- even though vulkaninfo
(same ICD, same physical device, same WSI layer) reports hasPrimary=true / hasRender=true
(primaryMinor=1 -> /dev/dri/card1, renderMinor=128 -> /dev/dri/renderD128, both present).
The extension IS advertised (hasDrmProps=true) and the function pointer is resolved via
vkGetInstanceProcAddr (instance is API 1.3), so the query *should* populate the struct --
but it doesn't. This is a gamescope 3.16.19 query interop quirk, not a driver/ICD/node
issue. (Driver 580 alone does NOT fix it; driver 595 additionally breaks the libGLX ICD
for headless -- see UPCLOUD-L4-DEPLOY-2026-07.md blocker #1 for that separate fix.)

The headless backend does no KMS scanout, so it genuinely does NOT need a primary DRM
node. The render node IS needed (m_drmRendererFd -> drm syncobjs in Timeline.cpp), but
when the query returns zeros we can fall back to scanning /dev/dri/renderD* (the CDI-
injected nvidia render node) and open it directly.

This patch:
  1. Relaxes the headless !drmProps.hasPrimary abort to a warning (continue without a
     primary dev id -- the existing `if (drmProps.hasPrimary)` guard already handles
     hasPrimary=false gracefully for m_drmPrimaryDevId; and vulkan_primary_dev_id() is
     only called from DRMBackend.cpp, which the headless backend never uses).
  2. Wraps the render-node acquisition in `if (drmProps.hasRender) {normal
     drmGetDeviceFromDevId path} else {/dev/dri/renderD* scan fallback}` so the headless
     backend can still obtain m_drmRendererFd when the query returns zeros.

Apply on top of the 3v1n0 gamescope 3.16.19 source (`apt-get source gamescope` on noble
with the 3v1n0 PPA + deb-src enabled) and rebuild with `meson setup build && ninja -C
build`. Install build/src/{gamescope,gamescopereaper,gamescopestream,gamescopectl} over
the deb's /usr/games/ binaries.

A SEPARATE prerequisite: the dpad user must be able to open /dev/dri/renderD128. Some
hosts map the nvidia render node's GID to an unexpected group (UpCloud: GID 993 =
`polkitd` in the container, while dpad is only in video/audio/input). The entrypoint
must ensure dpad is in the render node's owning group (or chmod the node) -- see the
UPCLOUD-L4-DEPLOY-2026-07.md render-node permissions fix.

